  "hypothesis": "Missing repeated create_des_coder calls may indicate missing or repeated initialization in JS public level-construction methods.",
  "expectedBehavior": "Under normal successful loader ordering, selected C guards are no-ops after initial creation; JS public calls preserve deliberately changed coder-owned level flags.",
  "observedBehavior": "Source hashes/order checks pin C load_special and six guards, plus JS constructor initialization before API registration. Exact C create_des_coder runs6 times with an initialized coder:0 initializer calls and unchanged pointer/marker. Production JS level_flags,level_init,terrain,wall_property,exclusion,teleport_region sequence preserves deliberately set rndmongen0/deathdrops0/temperature-1 after every call.",
  "witness": {
    "kind": "source",
    "scope": "Source hashes/order checks pin C load_special and six guards, plus JS constructor initialization before API registration. Exact C create_des_coder runs6 times with an initialized coder:0 initializer calls and unchanged pointer/marker. Production JS level_flags,level_init,terrain,wall_property,exclusion,teleport_region sequence preserves deliberately set rndmongen0/deathdrops0/temperature-1 after every call.",
    "limitations": [
